From a4160b7908693319bb3d588c2974c0197f078011 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Turnover <nine925444@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 18:11:46 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Verify webhooks with Ring's HMAC X-Signature and accept all
 documented event types

Ring signs webhooks as X-Signature: sha256=<hex HMAC-SHA256 of the raw body>
using the app's HMAC Signing Key. The handler previously checked a Bearer
Authorization header, which Ring does not send, and its schema only allowed
motion_detected, device_added, device_removed and an undocumented
person_detected, so button_press, device_online/offline, app_integration_*
and subscription_* deliveries fell through to the generic path.

- verify X-Signature over the raw bytes before parsing (RING_HMAC_KEY),
  constant-time compare; keep RING_WEBHOOK_SECRET as a deprecated fallback
- accept every documented v1.1 event type, keep unknown types as strings
- add sub_type (open vocabulary), component_ids, timestamp_readable,
  meta.account_id, subscription device relationships
- device_id only when source_type is devices (app_integration_* carries the
  account ID in source)
- /api/webhook/test now signs a v1.1 payload and sends it through the real
  handler, so verification is exercised locally
- README and .env.example document RING_HMAC_KEY with an openssl recipe

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Eqje7FBkk9KJg8SkLLHajj
